{
  "_about": "API keys and tokens. Merged into every policy, including the base. Secret classifications start with secret-, and each rule's placeholder names its classification. Labels cover password, passwd, secret, secret_key, token, api_key, access_key, client_secret, private_key, security_key, app_key, db_pass and an underscore-suffixed pwd (a value starting with a slash is never taken as one). A PHP define() call whose name ends in PASSWORD, KEY, SALT or SECRET is caught on its own rule. There is deliberately no generic high-entropy rule: git SHAs, UUIDs and lockfile integrity hashes must pass through. Cases live in tests/cases/api_keys.py. Known gaps: a YAML-style line (colon separator) with an unquoted letters-only value is not caught; an unquoted value is caught only up to its first space, quote, & ; or , ; a URL password that starts with 1-5 digits and then ? or #, or has a further / ? # = or & between that digit prefix and the @, is read as host:port and not caught.",
